module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Flat
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.Germ
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.Independence
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Flat base change for Koszul-regular, `H₁`-regular and quasi-regular ideal sheaves

Stacks tag 067P says that a regular, Koszul-regular, `H₁`-regular or quasi-regular immersion
remains one after a **flat** base change.  (Flatness is not a convenience: for an arbitrary base
change the statement is false — `(x) ⊆ k[x]` is Koszul-regular, while its pullback
`(x̄) ⊆ k[x]/(x²)` is not, every generating sequence being annihilated by `x̄ ≠ 0`.)

Under Stacks tag 063G the conditions of Stacks tag 063J on an immersion are conditions of Stacks
tag 063D on a sheaf of ideals, and the base change of an immersion cuts out the *inverse image
ideal sheaf* `g^{-1}J · O_{X'}` of the ideal sheaf cutting out the immersion.  This file proves
067P in exactly that form: for the three conditions of Stacks tag 063D that are conditions on
germs — parts (2), (3) and (4), i.e. Koszul-regular, `H₁`-regular and quasi-regular — the inverse
image ideal sheaf along a morphism with flat stalk maps again satisfies the condition.

## Main definitions

* `HasFlatStalks h`: every stalk map of the morphism `h` is a flat ring map.  This is the
  stalkwise form of flatness, and for a morphism of schemes it is `AlgebraicGeometry.Flat`
  (`hasFlatStalks_of_flat`).
* `pullbackSections h U f`: the images under `h^♯` of sections of `U`, as sections of `h⁻¹U`.
* `pullbackIdeal h J`: **the inverse image ideal sheaf** `h^{-1}J · O_{X'}`, the ideal subsheaf of
  `O_{X'}` whose sections over `V` are those whose germ at each point `x` of `V` lies in the ideal
  of `O_{X',x}` generated by the image of the stalk `J_{h(x)}`.

## Main results

* `isKoszulRegular_algebraMap_of_flat`, `isH1Regular_algebraMap_of_flat` and
  `isQuasiRegularRel_algebraMap_of_flat`: the ring-level engines, flat base change for a
  Koszul-regular, `H₁`-regular or quasi-regular sequence *with coefficients in the base ring*.
  These are Stacks tags 062H and 065L specialised to the coefficient module `R`, which is the
  shape the germ conditions of Stacks tag 063D are stated in.
* `isKoszulSequenceExactOn_pullbackSections` and
  `forall_isQuasiRegularRel_germFamily_pullbackSections`: the germ conditions of Stacks tag 063D
  transport along a morphism with flat stalk maps, because the germs of the pulled-back sections
  are the images of the germs under the stalk map.
* `isGeneratedByOn_pullbackIdeal`: a generating sequence of `J` over `U` pulls back to a
  generating sequence of `pullbackIdeal h J` over `h⁻¹U`.
* `mem_idealQuotientSupport_of_mem_idealQuotientSupport_pullbackIdeal`: the support of
  `O_{X'}/h^{-1}J·O_{X'}` lies over the support of `O_X/J`.
* `isKoszulRegularIdealSheaf_pullbackIdeal`, `isH1RegularIdealSheaf_pullbackIdeal` and
  `isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf_pullbackIdeal`: **Stacks tag 067P**, parts (2), (3) and (4), at the
  level of ideal sheaves.

## Implementation notes

The three conditions are transported **germwise**, one point at a time, rather than globally: at
a point `x` of `X'` the stalk map `O_{X,h(x)} → O_{X',x}` is a flat ring map, the germs of the
pulled-back generators are the images of the germs of the generators
(`germFamily_pullbackSections`, which is `PresheafedSpace.stalkMap_germ`), and the ring-level
engines apply.  This is the same strategy that made the independence clause of Stacks tag 063J
tractable in `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.Independence`.

The inverse image ideal sheaf is defined germwise for the same reason: the condition
"the germ at every point lies in the image ideal" is automatically local, so no sheafification is
needed, and it is exactly the form the generation statement `IsGeneratedByOn` is proved in
(`mem_generatedIdealOn_iff`).

Part (1) of Stacks tag 063D, regularity, is monicity of a multiplication morphism of sheaves and
not a condition on germs, so it is not covered by the germ transport used here; part (1) of 067P
is not proved in this file.  The three parts proved here are stated for the inverse image ideal
sheaf.  Deducing the immersion-level statement of Stacks tag 063J from them additionally needs the
identification of the defining ideal sheaf of the base-changed immersion with the inverse image
ideal sheaf of the defining ideal sheaf, which this development does not yet have.

The flat hypothesis is taken stalkwise (`HasFlatStalks`) rather than as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Flat`, because the conditions of Stacks tag 063D are conditions on stalks and
because the statement then applies to a morphism of locally ringed spaces.  For a morphism of
schemes the two agree, by `AlgebraicGeometry.Flat.iff_flat_stalkMap`; `hasFlatStalks_of_flat`
records the direction needed here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.21.14 (Tag 067P)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/067P)
* [Stacks Project, Definition 31.21.2 (Tag 063D)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063D)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 15.31.5 (Tag 062H)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/062H)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 10.69.5 (Tag 065L)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/065L)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular
open Stacks.RingTheory.QuasiRegular
open Stacks.RingTheory.RegularIdealSheaf
open scoped ExteriorAlgebra TensorProduct
open Stacks.RingedSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

/-! ### Flat base change for the ring-level conditions -/

section RingLevel

variable {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] {r : ℕ}

/-- Changing the coefficient module of the Koszul complex by a linear equivalence leaves its
homology isomorphic.  The two complexes may live in different `ModuleCat` universes, so the
transport is the explicit one of `KoszulC.homologyTransport_of_degreewiseEquiv` rather than a
categorical `homologyMapIso`. -/
private theorem nonempty_koszulHomology_equiv_of_coefficients (g : Fin r → S)
    {M N : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module S M] [AddCommGroup N] [Module S N]
    (e : M ≃ₗ[S] N) (i : ℕ) :
    Nonempty ((Koszul.seqComplexTensor g M).homology i ≃ₗ[S]
      (Koszul.seqComplexTensor g N).homology i) := by
  refine KoszulC.homologyTransport_of_degreewiseEquiv
    (fun n => e.lTensor (⋀[S]^n (Fin r → S))) ?_ i
  intro n m x
  by_cases hnm : m + 1 = n
  · subst hnm
    rw [Koszul.seqComplexTensor_d, Koszul.seqComplexTensor_d]
    have he : (e.lTensor (⋀[S]^m (Fin r → S))).toLinearMap ∘ₗ
          (Koszul.d (Koszul.seqDual g) m).rTensor M =
        (Koszul.d (Koszul.seqDual g) m).rTensor N ∘ₗ
          (e.lTensor (⋀[S]^(m + 1) (Fin r → S))).toLinearMap := by
      apply TensorProduct.ext
      ext a b
      rfl
    exact LinearMap.congr_fun he x
  · rw [(Koszul.seqComplexTensor g M).shape n m hnm,
      (Koszul.seqComplexTensor g N).shape n m hnm]
    exact (e.lTensor (⋀[S]^m (Fin r → S))).toLinearMap.map_zero

/-- **Flat base change for Koszul homology in a fixed degree, with coefficients in the base
ring.** This is Stacks tag 062H for the coefficient module `R`, the shape in which the conditions
of Stacks tag 063D are stated: the conclusion of `KoszulC.homology_isZero_baseChange` has
coefficients `S ⊗[R] R`, which the right unitor identifies with `S`. -/
private theorem isZero_koszulHomology_algebraMap [Module.Flat R S] (f : Fin r → R) (i : ℕ)
    (h : IsZero ((Koszul.seqComplex f).homology i)) :
    IsZero ((Koszul.seqComplex (fun j => algebraMap R S (f j))).homology i) := by
  have h0 : IsZero ((Koszul.seqComplexTensor f R).homology i) :=
    h.of_iso (Koszul.homologySelfIso f i)
  rw [ModuleCat.isZero_iff_subsingleton] at h0
  have h1 := KoszulC.homology_baseChange_subsingleton (S := S) f R i h0
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_koszulHomology_equiv_of_coefficients
    (fun j => algebraMap R S (f j)) (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.rid R S S) i
  have h2 : Subsingleton ((Koszul.seqComplexTensor (R := S)
      (fun j => algebraMap R S (f j)) S).homology i) := e.symm.toEquiv.subsingleton
  have h3 : IsZero ((Koszul.seqComplexTensor (R := S)
      (fun j => algebraMap R S (f j)) S).homology i) :=
    ModuleCat.isZero_iff_subsingleton.mpr h2
  exact h3.of_iso (Koszul.homologySelfIso (R := S) (fun j => algebraMap R S (f j)) i).symm

/-- Flat base change for Koszul homology, stated for any sequence equal to the image sequence.
Phrasing it this way avoids rewriting under the `HasHomology` instance of the Koszul complex,
whose type depends on the sequence. -/
private theorem isZero_koszulHomology_of_eq_algebraMap [Module.Flat R S] (f : Fin r → R)
    (g : Fin r → S) (hg : (fun j => algebraMap R S (f j)) = g) (i : ℕ)
    (h : IsZero ((Koszul.seqComplex f).homology i)) :
    IsZero ((Koszul.seqComplex g).homology i) := by
  subst hg
  exact isZero_koszulHomology_algebraMap f i h

/-- **Flat base change for a Koszul-regular sequence, Stacks tag 062H part (2), with coefficients
in the base ring.** -/
theorem isKoszulRegular_algebraMap_of_flat [Module.Flat R S] (f : Fin r → R)
    (h : Koszul.IsKoszulRegular f) :
    Koszul.IsKoszulRegular (fun j => algebraMap R S (f j)) :=
  fun i hi => isZero_koszulHomology_algebraMap f i (h i hi)

/-- **Flat base change for an `H₁`-regular sequence, Stacks tag 062H part (1), with coefficients
in the base ring.** -/
theorem isH1Regular_algebraMap_of_flat [Module.Flat R S] (f : Fin r → R)
    (h : Koszul.IsH1Regular f) :
    Koszul.IsH1Regular (fun j => algebraMap R S (f j)) :=
  isZero_koszulHomology_algebraMap f 1 h

/-- **Flat base change for a quasi-regular sequence, Stacks tag 065L, in the elementary relation
form and with coefficients in the base ring.** The base change of `R` to `S` is `S` itself, which
is what `IsBaseChange.linearMap` records. -/
theorem isQuasiRegularRel_algebraMap_of_flat [Module.Flat R S] (f : Fin r → R)
    (h : IsQuasiRegularRel f) :
    IsQuasiRegularRel (fun j => algebraMap R S (f j)) := by
  rw [isQuasiRegularRel_iff_bijective] at h
  rw [isQuasiRegularRel_iff_bijective, ← isQuasiRegular_ofFn_iff]
  have hqr := RingTheory.Sequence.IsQuasiRegular.of_flat_of_isBaseChange (N := S)
    (IsBaseChange.linearMap (R := R) (S := S)) (rs := List.ofFn f)
    ((isQuasiRegular_ofFn_iff f).mpr h)
  rwa [List.map_ofFn] at hqr

end RingLevel

/-! ### Morphisms with flat stalk maps -/

section Pullback

variable {X' X : LocallyRingedSpace.{u}} (h : X' ⟶ X)

/-- **A morphism with flat stalk maps.** The stalkwise form of flatness: every stalk map
`O_{X,h(x)} → O_{X',x}` is a flat ring map.  The conditions of Stacks tag 063D that this file
transports are conditions on stalks, so this is the hypothesis they need. -/
def HasFlatStalks : Prop :=
  ∀ x : X', (LocallyRingedSpace.Hom.stalkMap h x).hom.Flat

/-- **The pulled-back sections.** The images under `h^♯` of sections of `O_X` over `U`, as
sections of `O_{X'}` over `h⁻¹U`. -/
noncomputable def pullbackSections (U : Opens X) {r : ℕ}
    (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)) :
    Fin r → X'.presheaf.obj (op ((Opens.map h.base).obj U)) :=
  fun i => h.c.app (op U) (f i)

/-- The germ of a pulled-back section is the image of the germ under the stalk map. -/
theorem germFamily_pullbackSections (U : Opens X) {r : ℕ}
    (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)) (x : X') (hx : h.base x ∈ U) (i : Fin r) :
    germFamily X'.toRingedSpace ((Opens.map h.base).obj U)
        (pullbackSections h U f) x hx i
      = LocallyRingedSpace.Hom.stalkMap h x
          (germFamily X.toRingedSpace U f (h.base x) hx i) :=
  (AlgebraicGeometry.PresheafedSpace.stalkMap_germ_apply h.toHom U x hx (f i)).symm

/-- The germs of the pulled-back sections are the images of the germs under the stalk map. -/
private theorem germFamily_pullbackSections_eq (U : Opens X) {r : ℕ}
    (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)) (x : X') (hx : h.base x ∈ U) :
    germFamily X'.toRingedSpace ((Opens.map h.base).obj U) (pullbackSections h U f) x hx
      = fun i => (LocallyRingedSpace.Hom.stalkMap h x).hom
          (germFamily X.toRingedSpace U f (h.base x) hx i) :=
  funext fun i => germFamily_pullbackSections h U f x hx i

/-- **The germ conditions of Stacks tag 063D parts (2) and (3) transport along a morphism with
flat stalk maps.** Exactness of the Koszul complex of a sequence of sections in a set of degrees
is inherited by the pulled-back sequence, degree by degree and point by point, from flat base
change for the Koszul complex (Stacks tag 062H). -/
theorem isKoszulSequenceExactOn_pullbackSections (hflat : HasFlatStalks h) (U : Opens X) {r : ℕ}
    (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)) (P : ℕ → Prop)
    (hf : IsKoszulSequenceExactOn X.toRingedSpace U f P) :
    IsKoszulSequenceExactOn X'.toRingedSpace ((Opens.map h.base).obj U)
      (pullbackSections h U f) P := by
  intro x hx j hj
  have hfl := hflat x
  algebraize [(LocallyRingedSpace.Hom.stalkMap h x).hom]
  exact isZero_koszulHomology_of_eq_algebraMap (S := X'.presheaf.stalk x) _ _
    (germFamily_pullbackSections_eq h U f x hx).symm j (hf (h.base x) hx j hj)

/-- **The germ condition of Stacks tag 063D part (4) transports along a morphism with flat stalk
maps.** The elementary relation form of quasi-regularity is inherited by the germs of the
pulled-back sequence, from flat base change for quasi-regular sequences (Stacks tag 065L). -/
theorem forall_isQuasiRegularRel_germFamily_pullbackSections (hflat : HasFlatStalks h)
    (U : Opens X) {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U))
    (hf : ∀ (y : X) (hy : y ∈ U), IsQuasiRegularRel (germFamily X.toRingedSpace U f y hy)) :
    ∀ (x : X') (hx : x ∈ (Opens.map h.base).obj U),
      IsQuasiRegularRel (germFamily X'.toRingedSpace
        ((Opens.map h.base).obj U) (pullbackSections h U f) x hx) := by
  intro x hx
  have hfl := hflat x
  algebraize [(LocallyRingedSpace.Hom.stalkMap h x).hom]
  exact isQuasiRegularRel_congr (germFamily_pullbackSections_eq h U f x hx).symm
    (isQuasiRegularRel_algebraMap_of_flat (S := X'.presheaf.stalk x) _ (hf (h.base x) hx))

/-! ### The inverse image ideal sheaf -/

/-- The ideal of sections of `O_{X'}` over `V` whose germ at each point `x` of `V` lies in the
ideal generated by the image of the stalk of `J` at `h(x)`. -/
noncomputable def pullbackIdealObj (J : (structureSheafModule X.toRingedSpace).Submodule)
    (V : Opens X') : Ideal (X'.presheaf.obj (op V)) where
  carrier := {s | ∀ (x : X') (hx : x ∈ V),
    X'.presheaf.germ V x hx s ∈ Ideal.map (LocallyRingedSpace.Hom.stalkMap h x).hom
      (Stacks.RingedSpace.stalkIdeal J (h.base x))}
  zero_mem' x hx := by rw [map_zero]; exact Ideal.zero_mem _
  add_mem' {a b} ha hb x hx := by
    rw [map_add]; exact Ideal.add_mem _ (ha x hx) (hb x hx)
  smul_mem' c a ha x hx := by
    rw [smul_eq_mul, map_mul]; exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (ha x hx)

/-- **The inverse image ideal sheaf** `h^{-1}J · O_{X'}`.  Over an open `V` its sections are those
whose germ at each point `x` of `V` lies in the ideal of `O_{X',x}` generated by the image of the
stalk `J_{h(x)}`.  No sheafification is needed: a condition on germs is local. -/
noncomputable def pullbackIdeal (J : (structureSheafModule X.toRingedSpace).Submodule) :
    (structureSheafModule X'.toRingedSpace).Submodule where
  toSubmodule :=
    { obj V := pullbackIdealObj h J V.unop
      map {V W} i s hs x hxW := by
        have hg : X'.presheaf.germ W.unop x hxW (X'.presheaf.map i s)
            = X'.presheaf.germ V.unop x (i.unop.le hxW) s :=
          TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply' X'.presheaf i x hxW s
        exact hg ▸ hs x (i.unop.le hxW) }
  isSheaf {V} s hsieve x hxV := by
    obtain ⟨W, g, hgs, hxW⟩ := (Opens.mem_grothendieckTopology _).mp hsieve x hxV
    have hg : X'.presheaf.germ W x hxW (X'.presheaf.map g.op s)
        = X'.presheaf.germ V.unop x (g.le hxW) s :=
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply X'.presheaf g x hxW s
    exact hg ▸ hgs x hxW

/-- A section `s` of `O_{X'}` over `V` lies in `pullbackIdeal h J` if and only if its germ at every
point `x` of `V` lies in the ideal of `O_{X',x}` generated by the image of the stalk `J_{h(x)}`. -/
theorem mem_pullbackIdeal {J : (structureSheafModule X.toRingedSpace).Submodule} (V : Opens X')
    (s : X'.presheaf.obj (op V)) :
    s ∈ (pullbackIdeal h J).obj (op V) ↔
      ∀ (x : X') (hx : x ∈ V),
        X'.presheaf.germ V x hx s ∈ Ideal.map (LocallyRingedSpace.Hom.stalkMap h x).hom
          (Stacks.RingedSpace.stalkIdeal J (h.base x)) :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- At a point over `U`, the image of the stalk of `J` is the ideal generated by the germs of the
pulled-back generators.  This is `stalkIdeal_eq_Jid_germFamily` followed by `Jid_map`. -/
theorem map_stalkIdeal_eq_Jid_germFamily_pullbackSections
    {J : (structureSheafModule X.toRingedSpace).Submodule} (U : Opens X) {r : ℕ}
    (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)) (hgen : IsGeneratedByOn X.toRingedSpace J U f)
    (x : X') (hx : h.base x ∈ U) :
    Ideal.map (LocallyRingedSpace.Hom.stalkMap h x).hom
        (Stacks.RingedSpace.stalkIdeal J (h.base x))
      = Jid (germFamily X'.toRingedSpace ((Opens.map h.base).obj U)
          (pullbackSections h U f) x hx) := by
  rw [germFamily_pullbackSections_eq, Jid_map (LocallyRingedSpace.Hom.stalkMap h x).hom,
    stalkIdeal_eq_Jid_germFamily J U f hgen (h.base x) hx]

/-- **A generating sequence pulls back to a generating sequence of the inverse image ideal
sheaf.** -/
theorem isGeneratedByOn_pullbackIdeal
    {J : (structureSheafModule X.toRingedSpace).Submodule} (U : Opens X) {r : ℕ}
    (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)) (hgen : IsGeneratedByOn X.toRingedSpace J U f) :
    IsGeneratedByOn X'.toRingedSpace (pullbackIdeal h J)
      ((Opens.map h.base).obj U) (pullbackSections h U f) := by
  intro V hVU
  refine Submodule.ext fun s =>
    Iff.trans
      (forall_congr' fun x => forall_congr' fun hx =>
        iff_of_eq (congrArg (fun I : Ideal (X'.presheaf.stalk x) =>
            X'.presheaf.germ V x hx s ∈ I)
          (map_stalkIdeal_eq_Jid_germFamily_pullbackSections h U f hgen x (hVU hx))))
      (mem_generatedIdealOn_iff (X := X'.toRingedSpace) ((Opens.map h.base).obj U)
        (pullbackSections h U f) V hVU s).symm

/-- **The support of the quotient by the inverse image ideal sheaf lies over the support of the
quotient by `J`.** If `J` contains the unit section near `h(x)` then the inverse image ideal sheaf
contains it near `x`. -/
theorem mem_idealQuotientSupport_of_mem_idealQuotientSupport_pullbackIdeal
    (J : (structureSheafModule X.toRingedSpace).Submodule) (x : X')
    (hx : x ∈ idealQuotientSupport X'.toRingedSpace (pullbackIdeal h J)) :
    h.base x ∈ idealQuotientSupport X.toRingedSpace J := by
  by_contra hcon
  obtain ⟨U, hU, h1⟩ :=
    (notMem_idealQuotientSupport_iff J (h.base x)).mp hcon
  refine notMem_idealQuotientSupport_of_one_mem (pullbackIdeal h J) x
    ((Opens.map h.base).obj U) hU (fun y hy => ?_) hx
  have htop : Stacks.RingedSpace.stalkIdeal J (h.base y) = ⊤ :=
    Ideal.eq_top_iff_one _ |>.mpr
      (Ideal.subset_span ⟨U, hy, 1, h1, map_one _⟩)
  rw [map_one, htop, Ideal.map_top]
  trivial

/-! ### Stacks tag 067P, parts (2), (3) and (4) -/

/-- The inverse image ideal sheaf inherits a local generating sequence with Koszul exactness in the
degrees `P`. -/
private theorem exists_koszulSequenceExactOn_pullbackIdeal (hflat : HasFlatStalks h)
    (J : (structureSheafModule X.toRingedSpace).Submodule) (P : ℕ → Prop)
    (hJ : ∀ x : X, x ∈ idealQuotientSupport X.toRingedSpace J →
      ∃ (U : Opens X) (_ : x ∈ U) (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)),
        IsKoszulSequenceExactOn X.toRingedSpace U f P ∧ IsGeneratedByOn X.toRingedSpace J U f)
    (x : X') (hx : x ∈ idealQuotientSupport X'.toRingedSpace (pullbackIdeal h J)) :
    ∃ (U : Opens X') (_ : x ∈ U) (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → X'.presheaf.obj (op U)),
      IsKoszulSequenceExactOn X'.toRingedSpace U f P ∧
        IsGeneratedByOn X'.toRingedSpace (pullbackIdeal h J) U f := by
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, r, f, hK, hG⟩ := hJ (h.base x)
    (mem_idealQuotientSupport_of_mem_idealQuotientSupport_pullbackIdeal h J x hx)
  exact ⟨(Opens.map h.base).obj U, hxU, r, pullbackSections h U f,
    isKoszulSequenceExactOn_pullbackSections h hflat U f _ hK,
    isGeneratedByOn_pullbackIdeal h U f hG⟩

/-- **Stacks tag 067P, part (2), at the level of ideal sheaves.** The inverse image ideal sheaf
of a Koszul-regular ideal sheaf along a morphism with flat stalk maps is Koszul-regular. -/
@[stacks 067P "part (2), ideal-sheaf level: the inverse image ideal sheaf `h⁻¹J·O_{X'}` of a \
Koszul-regular ideal sheaf along a morphism of locally ringed spaces with flat stalk maps is \
Koszul-regular", sga "6 VII 1.5" "flat base change, Koszul"]
theorem isKoszulRegularIdealSheaf_pullbackIdeal (hflat : HasFlatStalks h)
    (J : (structureSheafModule X.toRingedSpace).Submodule)
    (hJ : IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf X.toRingedSpace J) :
    IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf X'.toRingedSpace (pullbackIdeal h J) := by
  exact exists_koszulSequenceExactOn_pullbackIdeal h hflat J _ hJ

/-- **Stacks tag 067P, part (3), at the level of ideal sheaves.** The inverse image ideal sheaf
of an `H₁`-regular ideal sheaf along a morphism with flat stalk maps is `H₁`-regular. -/
@[stacks 067P "part (3), ideal-sheaf level: the inverse image ideal sheaf `h⁻¹J·O_{X'}` of an \
H₁-regular ideal sheaf along a morphism of locally ringed spaces with flat stalk maps is \
H₁-regular", sga "6 VII 1.5" "flat base change, H1"]
theorem isH1RegularIdealSheaf_pullbackIdeal (hflat : HasFlatStalks h)
    (J : (structureSheafModule X.toRingedSpace).Submodule)
    (hJ : IsH1RegularIdealSheaf X.toRingedSpace J) :
    IsH1RegularIdealSheaf X'.toRingedSpace (pullbackIdeal h J) := by
  exact exists_koszulSequenceExactOn_pullbackIdeal h hflat J _ hJ

/-- **Stacks tag 067P, part (4), at the level of ideal sheaves.** The inverse image ideal sheaf
of a quasi-regular ideal sheaf along a morphism with flat stalk maps is quasi-regular. -/
@[stacks 067P "part (4), ideal-sheaf level: the inverse image ideal sheaf `h⁻¹J·O_{X'}` of a \
quasi-regular ideal sheaf along a morphism of locally ringed spaces with flat stalk maps is \
quasi-regular", sga "6 VII 1.5" "flat base change, quasi"]
theorem isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf_pullbackIdeal (hflat : HasFlatStalks h)
    (J : (structureSheafModule X.toRingedSpace).Submodule)
    (hJ : IsQuasiRegularIdealSheaf X.toRingedSpace J) :
    IsQuasiRegularIdealSheaf X'.toRingedSpace (pullbackIdeal h J) := by
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, r, f, hiso, hG⟩ := hJ (h.base x)
    (mem_idealQuotientSupport_of_mem_idealQuotientSupport_pullbackIdeal h J x hx)
  refine ⟨(Opens.map h.base).obj U, hxU, r, pullbackSections h U f, ?_,
    isGeneratedByOn_pullbackIdeal h U f hG⟩
  rw [isQuasiRegularMapIso_iff_forall_germ]
  exact forall_isQuasiRegularRel_germFamily_pullbackSections h hflat U f
    ((isQuasiRegularMapIso_iff_forall_germ X.toRingedSpace U f).mp hiso)

end Pullback

/-! ### Flatness for a morphism of schemes -/

section Schemes

/-- A flat morphism of schemes has flat stalk maps: this is one direction of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Flat.iff_flat_stalkMap`. -/
theorem hasFlatStalks_of_flat {X' X : Scheme.{u}} (g : X' ⟶ X) [AlgebraicGeometry.Flat g] :
    HasFlatStalks g.toLRSHom :=
  fun x => AlgebraicGeometry.Flat.stalkMap g x

end Schemes

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

